<p>The plugin ships types for Drupal's JavaScript API and generates a TypeScript setup for your theme.</p>

<h2>Setup</h2>
<p>The <code>uebertool</code> binary, which runs before <code>vite</code> in the <code>dev</code> and <code>build</code> scripts, writes <code>.uebertool/tsconfig.json</code> and <code>.uebertool/vite-env.d.ts</code>. Extend it from your theme:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'json', title: 'tsconfig.json' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
{
  "extends": "./.uebertool/tsconfig.json"
}
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% include code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: generated.vite_env.path, code: generated.vite_env.code } only %}

<h2>What is typed</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>Drupal</code>: behaviors, <code>Drupal.t()</code>, <code>Drupal.Message</code>, … and <code>drupalSettings</code>,</li>
  <li><code>once()</code> from <code>core/once</code>,</li>
  <li>Vite's <code>import.meta.env</code> and <code>import.meta.hot</code>,</li>
  <li><code>*.vue</code> imports,</li>
  <li><a href="{{ path('uebertool_docs_pages.page', { slug: 'auto-imports' }) }}">auto-imports</a> and Vue custom element tag names (<code>.uebertool/*.d.ts</code>).</li>
</ul>

{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
Drupal.behaviors.accordion = {
  attach(context) {
    once('accordion', '.accordion', context).forEach((element) => {
      element.setAttribute('aria-label', Drupal.t('Accordion'))
    })
  },
}
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

